1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,020
You have learned eight things about SonarQube. But can you prove it?

2
00:00:04,570 --> 00:00:09,267
A demo that works on a video is not the same as a skill that works for you.

3
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:10,144
In a real job,

4
00:00:10,144 --> 00:00:13,840
someone will ask: is the quality gate really protecting us?

5
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:14,341
Show me.

6
00:00:14,891 --> 00:00:16,340
So today is different.

7
00:00:16,340 --> 00:00:18,647
We build one real quality pipeline,

8
00:00:18,647 --> 00:00:19,503
from nothing,

9
00:00:19,503 --> 00:00:22,139
and a script checks it with seven tests.

10
00:00:22,139 --> 00:00:23,194
Each one passes,

11
00:00:23,194 --> 00:00:23,787
or fails.

12
00:00:24,337 --> 00:00:25,215
Seven of seven,

13
00:00:25,215 --> 00:00:27,089
and you have mastered SonarQube.

14
00:00:27,089 --> 00:00:28,904
Then we write down the results,

15
00:00:28,904 --> 00:00:29,841
and we clean up.

16
00:00:31,391 --> 00:00:32,820
Here is what to expect.

17
00:00:33,370 --> 00:00:36,229
One: the whole SonarQube domain, on one page.

18
00:00:36,779 --> 00:00:39,062
Two: the scenario, and the seven checks.

19
00:00:39,612 --> 00:00:40,825
Three: a live demo,

20
00:00:40,825 --> 00:00:43,508
in the real SonarQube and Jenkins screens,

21
00:00:43,508 --> 00:00:44,978
and in a real terminal.

22
00:00:44,978 --> 00:00:45,744
We build it,

23
00:00:45,744 --> 00:00:47,213
we break it on purpose,

24
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:47,852
we fix it,

25
00:00:47,852 --> 00:00:48,619
we check it,

26
00:00:48,619 --> 00:00:49,896
we keep the results,

27
00:00:49,896 --> 00:00:50,918
and we clean up.

28
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:54,754
Four: what to do when a check fails, and where to find the lab.

29
00:00:55,304 --> 00:00:58,525
This is the mastery lesson of the SonarQube domain.

30
00:01:00,075 --> 00:01:04,491
The SonarQube domain, on one page. Eight objectives, eight lessons.

31
00:01:05,041 --> 00:01:06,462
One: static analysis,

32
00:01:06,462 --> 00:01:07,409
quality gates,

33
00:01:07,409 --> 00:01:08,762
profiles and issues.

34
00:01:08,762 --> 00:01:10,522
Two: install a lab server,

35
00:01:10,522 --> 00:01:11,740
and connect to it.

36
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:14,368
Three: scan a Maven project.

37
00:01:14,368 --> 00:01:15,555
Four: read bugs,

38
00:01:15,555 --> 00:01:16,742
vulnerabilities,

39
00:01:16,742 --> 00:01:17,410
hotspots,

40
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:19,266
duplication and coverage.

41
00:01:19,816 --> 00:01:21,512
Five: build a quality gate,

42
00:01:21,512 --> 00:01:22,769
and know its limits.

43
00:01:22,769 --> 00:01:25,533
Six: put the scan and the gate into Jenkins.

44
00:01:26,083 --> 00:01:31,480
Seven: tokens and permissions. Eight: diagnose failures, by reading the first error.

45
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:35,017
Today one scenario uses the heart of all eight.

46
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:37,436
The scenario.

47
00:01:37,436 --> 00:01:40,243
A CloudCart pipeline that stops weak code,

48
00:01:40,243 --> 00:01:41,178
and proves it.

49
00:01:41,178 --> 00:01:42,047
Seven checks,

50
00:01:42,047 --> 00:01:43,116
run by a script.

51
00:01:43,666 --> 00:01:49,874
One: SonarQube is up. Two: your own gate, Cloud Cart gate, requires coverage of sixty two.

52
00:01:50,424 --> 00:01:55,480
Three: a web hook calls Jenkins back. Four: the coverage is sixty two or more.

53
00:01:56,030 --> 00:02:01,513
Five: the gate for the project says OK. Six: the last Jenkins build is a success.

54
00:02:02,063 --> 00:02:07,098
Seven: no token in the code. That last one is a trap, and we will fall in it on purpose.

55
00:02:07,648 --> 00:02:11,786
The script checks the facts, not your word. That is what makes it independent.

56
00:02:12,336 --> 00:02:14,192
Seven of seven, is mastery.

57
00:02:15,742 --> 00:02:16,937
A real SonarQube,

58
00:02:16,937 --> 00:02:18,835
signed in as administrator.

59
00:02:18,835 --> 00:02:20,733
The projects page is empty.

60
00:02:20,733 --> 00:02:21,787
No project yet,

61
00:02:21,787 --> 00:02:23,966
and no quality gate of our own.

62
00:02:23,966 --> 00:02:25,513
We start from nothing.

63
00:02:27,863 --> 00:02:28,256
First,

64
00:02:28,256 --> 00:02:29,108
the terminal.

65
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:31,008
The lab command is installed.

66
00:02:31,008 --> 00:02:33,302
Lab up checks that SonarQube is up,

67
00:02:33,302 --> 00:02:34,678
that Jenkins answers,

68
00:02:34,678 --> 00:02:36,972
and says where the results will go.

69
00:02:37,522 --> 00:02:38,816
Now the check script.

70
00:02:38,816 --> 00:02:40,787
Lab check runs the seven checks.

71
00:02:40,787 --> 00:02:42,080
Nothing is built yet,

72
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:43,374
so most of them fail,

73
00:02:43,374 --> 00:02:46,084
and every failure tells you what to do next.

74
00:02:46,084 --> 00:02:49,718
Look at the last one: it says there is a token in the code.

75
00:02:49,718 --> 00:02:51,197
We will come back to it.

76
00:02:57,747 --> 00:03:01,907
Step one: the quality gate. In SonarQube, we open Quality Gates.

77
00:03:06,957 --> 00:03:08,641
The default is Sonar way,

78
00:03:08,641 --> 00:03:10,527
and it only judges new code.

79
00:03:10,527 --> 00:03:12,414
We never change the default.

80
00:03:12,414 --> 00:03:13,491
We make our own.

81
00:03:13,491 --> 00:03:13,828
Copy,

82
00:03:13,828 --> 00:03:15,917
and we name it Cloud Cart gate.

83
00:03:21,967 --> 00:03:23,217
Then Add Condition.

84
00:03:23,217 --> 00:03:25,585
A condition is one rule of the gate.

85
00:03:25,585 --> 00:03:27,099
We choose overall code,

86
00:03:27,099 --> 00:03:29,796
because we want the whole project judged,

87
00:03:29,796 --> 00:03:31,309
not only the new lines.

88
00:03:31,309 --> 00:03:32,888
The measure is Coverage.

89
00:03:32,888 --> 00:03:35,125
And the rule: less than sixty two.

90
00:03:35,125 --> 00:03:35,849
Below that,

91
00:03:35,849 --> 00:03:36,836
the gate fails.

92
00:03:42,886 --> 00:03:44,598
And we make it the default,

93
00:03:44,598 --> 00:03:45,866
in the Actions menu,

94
00:03:45,866 --> 00:03:46,817
Set as Default.

95
00:03:46,817 --> 00:03:47,578
From now on,

96
00:03:47,578 --> 00:03:50,177
every new project is judged by this gate,

97
00:03:50,177 --> 00:03:51,762
unless we choose another.

98
00:03:51,762 --> 00:03:54,171
The project we scan next will meet it.

99
00:03:59,721 --> 00:04:01,303
Step two: the web hook.

100
00:04:01,303 --> 00:04:02,540
In Administration,

101
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:03,503
Configuration,

102
00:04:03,503 --> 00:04:04,191
Web hooks.

103
00:04:04,191 --> 00:04:07,904
A web hook is how SonarQube tells Jenkins the verdict.

104
00:04:07,904 --> 00:04:08,660
Without it,

105
00:04:08,660 --> 00:04:11,135
the gate stage never gets an answer.

106
00:04:11,135 --> 00:04:12,098
We create one.

107
00:04:12,098 --> 00:04:13,473
The name is jenkins,

108
00:04:13,473 --> 00:04:15,605
and the address is our Jenkins,

109
00:04:15,605 --> 00:04:16,980
with the last slash.

110
00:04:19,530 --> 00:04:21,298
Step three: the pipeline.

111
00:04:21,298 --> 00:04:22,077
In Jenkins,

112
00:04:22,077 --> 00:04:23,208
we open the job,

113
00:04:23,208 --> 00:04:24,552
cloud cart mastery.

114
00:04:24,552 --> 00:04:27,099
It has three stages: build and test,

115
00:04:27,099 --> 00:04:27,453
scan,

116
00:04:27,453 --> 00:04:28,938
and the quality gate.

117
00:04:28,938 --> 00:04:30,282
We click Build Now.

118
00:04:30,832 --> 00:04:32,160
We open the console.

119
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:33,620
Build and test passes.

120
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:35,015
The scan is accepted.

121
00:04:35,015 --> 00:04:37,272
Now Jenkins waits for the verdict,

122
00:04:37,272 --> 00:04:38,533
one minute at most.

123
00:04:39,083 --> 00:04:42,441
Here is what happens inside SonarQube while we wait.

124
00:04:42,441 --> 00:04:44,766
The compute engine takes the report,

125
00:04:44,766 --> 00:04:46,186
computes the measures,

126
00:04:46,186 --> 00:04:48,704
and checks every condition of the gate,

127
00:04:48,704 --> 00:04:49,415
one by one.

128
00:04:49,415 --> 00:04:51,610
Then SonarQube calls the web hook,

129
00:04:51,610 --> 00:04:53,547
and Jenkins hears the verdict.

130
00:04:54,097 --> 00:04:55,587
Two sides to this wait.

131
00:04:55,587 --> 00:04:57,271
SonarQube judges the code,

132
00:04:57,271 --> 00:04:59,927
and the web hook carries the answer back.

133
00:04:59,927 --> 00:05:00,898
Both must work.

134
00:05:00,898 --> 00:05:04,396
Remember lesson one seventy-one: without the web hook,

135
00:05:04,396 --> 00:05:05,756
this stage times out,

136
00:05:05,756 --> 00:05:06,663
with no error.

137
00:05:15,213 --> 00:05:15,492
Red.

138
00:05:15,492 --> 00:05:18,637
Pipeline aborted due to quality gate failure.

139
00:05:18,637 --> 00:05:20,454
This is not a broken tool.

140
00:05:20,454 --> 00:05:21,642
This is the gate,

141
00:05:21,642 --> 00:05:22,620
doing its job.

142
00:05:22,620 --> 00:05:24,087
We ask SonarQube why.

143
00:05:27,137 --> 00:05:28,277
The project page.

144
00:05:28,277 --> 00:05:28,746
Failed,

145
00:05:28,746 --> 00:05:32,499
with one condition: coverage is below sixty two percent.

146
00:05:32,499 --> 00:05:34,175
The gate wants sixty two,

147
00:05:34,175 --> 00:05:35,649
and the code has less.

148
00:05:40,199 --> 00:05:41,297
The fix is tests,

149
00:05:41,297 --> 00:05:42,394
not a lower gate.

150
00:05:42,394 --> 00:05:43,427
In the terminal,

151
00:05:43,427 --> 00:05:46,719
we copy the missing test file into the test folder.

152
00:05:46,719 --> 00:05:47,881
Then we commit it,

153
00:05:47,881 --> 00:05:48,720
with a short,

154
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,624
clear message.

155
00:05:49,624 --> 00:05:50,721
One small commit,

156
00:05:50,721 --> 00:05:52,722
so the history tells the story.

157
00:05:57,272 --> 00:06:01,880
Now we build again. We go back to the job, and click Build Now, one more time.

158
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:07,291
We open the console.

159
00:06:07,291 --> 00:06:08,243
While it runs,

160
00:06:08,243 --> 00:06:10,216
notice what we did not touch.

161
00:06:10,216 --> 00:06:11,372
Not the pipeline.

162
00:06:11,372 --> 00:06:12,257
Not the gate.

163
00:06:12,257 --> 00:06:13,209
Not SonarQube.

164
00:06:13,209 --> 00:06:14,638
We changed one thing,

165
00:06:14,638 --> 00:06:15,318
the tests,

166
00:06:15,318 --> 00:06:16,815
so if this goes green,

167
00:06:16,815 --> 00:06:18,175
we know exactly why.

168
00:06:18,725 --> 00:06:21,142
And notice what the pipeline is doing.

169
00:06:21,142 --> 00:06:22,350
It builds the code,

170
00:06:22,350 --> 00:06:23,622
and runs every test.

171
00:06:23,622 --> 00:06:26,611
Then it measures which lines the tests touched.

172
00:06:26,611 --> 00:06:27,693
That is coverage.

173
00:06:27,693 --> 00:06:29,664
The scan sends it to SonarQube,

174
00:06:29,664 --> 00:06:32,208
and the gate compares it with sixty two.

175
00:06:32,758 --> 00:06:34,657
Maven is slower than it looks.

176
00:06:34,657 --> 00:06:35,923
It runs forty tests,

177
00:06:35,923 --> 00:06:37,126
builds the package,

178
00:06:37,126 --> 00:06:39,974
and instruments the code to measure coverage.

179
00:06:39,974 --> 00:06:42,316
On a real project this takes minutes,

180
00:06:42,316 --> 00:06:45,734
which is why the scan comes only after the tests pass,

181
00:06:45,734 --> 00:06:48,139
and why the gate waits for the answer.

182
00:06:52,689 --> 00:06:57,020
The tests pass. The scan is accepted. The verdict arrives. And now, green.

183
00:07:02,070 --> 00:07:04,176
Look at the project in SonarQube.

184
00:07:04,176 --> 00:07:04,622
Passed,

185
00:07:04,622 --> 00:07:05,771
with a green mark.

186
00:07:05,771 --> 00:07:09,025
And the coverage on overall code is above the line.

187
00:07:11,075 --> 00:07:12,472
Back to the terminal.

188
00:07:12,472 --> 00:07:13,536
Lab check again.

189
00:07:13,536 --> 00:07:14,734
Six of seven pass.

190
00:07:14,734 --> 00:07:15,332
The gate,

191
00:07:15,332 --> 00:07:16,197
the web hook,

192
00:07:16,197 --> 00:07:17,062
the coverage,

193
00:07:17,062 --> 00:07:19,124
the project gate and the build.

194
00:07:19,124 --> 00:07:21,187
One fails: a token in the code.

195
00:07:21,737 --> 00:07:23,660
This is the troubleshooting.

196
00:07:23,660 --> 00:07:27,713
Leak check shows the file and the line: scripts/deploy.env.

197
00:07:27,713 --> 00:07:28,263
A token,

198
00:07:28,263 --> 00:07:30,186
committed in the repository.

199
00:07:30,186 --> 00:07:31,560
We treat it as real,

200
00:07:31,560 --> 00:07:32,659
so it is leaked.

201
00:07:33,209 --> 00:07:34,038
Two actions.

202
00:07:34,038 --> 00:07:34,452
First,

203
00:07:34,452 --> 00:07:36,109
remove it from the code.

204
00:07:36,109 --> 00:07:36,593
Second,

205
00:07:36,593 --> 00:07:38,181
revoke it in SonarQube,

206
00:07:38,181 --> 00:07:39,148
in My Account,

207
00:07:39,148 --> 00:07:39,769
Security,

208
00:07:39,769 --> 00:07:41,979
as we did in lesson one seventy.

209
00:07:41,979 --> 00:07:44,188
Removing the file is not enough,

210
00:07:44,188 --> 00:07:46,191
because the history keeps it.

211
00:07:46,191 --> 00:07:47,503
The token must die.

212
00:07:48,053 --> 00:07:51,999
Lab check one more time. Seven of seven. Every check passes.

213
00:07:52,549 --> 00:07:54,527
Results are part of the mastery.

214
00:07:54,527 --> 00:07:56,505
The script saved them in a file.

215
00:07:56,505 --> 00:07:57,062
Print it.

216
00:07:57,062 --> 00:07:58,978
This is your evidence: keep it,

217
00:07:58,978 --> 00:07:59,781
and share it.

218
00:08:00,331 --> 00:08:00,663
Last,

219
00:08:00,663 --> 00:08:01,458
the cleanup.

220
00:08:01,458 --> 00:08:03,379
Lab down deletes the project,

221
00:08:03,379 --> 00:08:04,241
the web hook,

222
00:08:04,241 --> 00:08:04,837
the gate,

223
00:08:04,837 --> 00:08:05,632
and the job.

224
00:08:05,632 --> 00:08:07,819
It keeps a copy of your evidence.

225
00:08:07,819 --> 00:08:10,337
SonarQube and Jenkins themselves stay.

226
00:08:10,887 --> 00:08:12,524
Run the check once more.

227
00:08:12,524 --> 00:08:13,479
Only two pass.

228
00:08:13,479 --> 00:08:14,775
SonarQube is alive,

229
00:08:14,775 --> 00:08:16,345
and your code is clean.

230
00:08:16,345 --> 00:08:17,777
The scenario is gone.

231
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:23,167
In the browser,

232
00:08:23,167 --> 00:08:25,454
the projects page is empty again.

233
00:08:25,454 --> 00:08:26,493
And in Jenkins,

234
00:08:26,493 --> 00:08:27,602
the job is gone.

235
00:08:27,602 --> 00:08:28,018
Built,

236
00:08:28,018 --> 00:08:28,503
broken,

237
00:08:28,503 --> 00:08:28,918
fixed,

238
00:08:28,918 --> 00:08:29,404
proved,

239
00:08:29,404 --> 00:08:30,304
written down,

240
00:08:30,304 --> 00:08:31,344
and cleaned up.

241
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:32,453
That is mastery.

242
00:08:34,003 --> 00:08:36,670
When a check fails, the message tells you where to look.

243
00:08:37,220 --> 00:08:41,636
One: SonarQube is not up. Run the start command, and wait for the word UP.

244
00:08:42,186 --> 00:08:43,667
Two: the gate is missing.

245
00:08:43,667 --> 00:08:44,851
The name must match,

246
00:08:44,851 --> 00:08:45,918
letter for letter,

247
00:08:45,918 --> 00:08:47,695
and the rule must be coverage,

248
00:08:47,695 --> 00:08:48,287
sixty two.

249
00:08:48,837 --> 00:08:53,680
Three: no web hook. Without it, the gate stage waits, and times out, with no error.

250
00:08:54,230 --> 00:08:58,048
Four: the coverage is low. Add tests. Do not lower the gate.

251
00:08:58,598 --> 00:09:03,505
Five: the gate says failed. Open the project page, and read the failing condition.

252
00:09:04,055 --> 00:09:07,980
Six: the build is red. Open the console, and read the first error.

253
00:09:08,530 --> 00:09:11,901
Seven: a token in the code. Remove it, and revoke it.

254
00:09:13,451 --> 00:09:16,246
Where to find the lab. Pause here, and write it down.

255
00:09:16,796 --> 00:09:25,030
One: the repository, github.com/it-waves/devops-ai, in the folder academy/lab.

256
00:09:25,580 --> 00:09:31,788
Two: the files, lab172.sh and shortcuts172.sh.

257
00:09:32,338 --> 00:09:37,778
Three: install it with sudo install, into /usr/local/sbin/.

258
00:09:38,328 --> 00:09:43,832
Four: load the short names with source shortcuts172.sh. Then lab up.

259
00:09:44,382 --> 00:09:50,206
Five: lab check runs the seven checks. Lab down cleans up. Leak check looks for tokens.

260
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:55,202
Six: you need the SonarQube and Jenkins from the earlier lessons.

261
00:09:55,202 --> 00:09:57,596
Set your user token in SONAR_TOKEN,

262
00:09:57,596 --> 00:09:59,716
and your login in JENKINS_AUTH.

263
00:10:00,266 --> 00:10:01,909
The link is in the description.

264
00:10:03,459 --> 00:10:05,230
Your turn, on your own machine.

265
00:10:05,780 --> 00:10:08,830
One: lab up, then lab check. See the failures first.

266
00:10:09,380 --> 00:10:11,343
Two: build your gate and your web hook.

267
00:10:11,893 --> 00:10:15,754
Three: build the pipeline, read the first failure, and add the tests.

268
00:10:16,304 --> 00:10:18,121
Four: find the leaked token,

269
00:10:18,121 --> 00:10:18,770
remove it,

270
00:10:18,770 --> 00:10:19,679
and revoke it.

271
00:10:19,679 --> 00:10:20,652
Then lab check,

272
00:10:20,652 --> 00:10:22,534
until you see seven of seven.

273
00:10:23,084 --> 00:10:26,774
Five: keep the results file as your evidence. Then lab down.

274
00:10:27,324 --> 00:10:29,052
Pause the video, and do it now.

275
00:10:44,602 --> 00:10:45,477
Quick check.

276
00:10:46,027 --> 00:10:48,160
Why does the gate stage need a web hook?

277
00:10:48,710 --> 00:10:51,974
